## 2. Fixed Attachment Duplication and Missing Files (Slack, Discord, ClickUp)

### Root Cause Analysis 

**Bug 1: Duplicated text and attachments on Slack and Discord when sent from Discord**
I found out that the root cause was ClickUp's webhook bouncing the attachments back to Slack and Discord. When our Node.js app uploads an attachment to a ClickUp task, ClickUp automatically generates a system message representing the uploaded file. This system message doesn't have the `[Author]` prefix prepended, so the loop-prevention logic in our [clickup.js](file:///e:/TDC_App/TDGAMES_App/Sync_Slack_Discord_ClickUp_Drive/test-clickup.js) webhook did not realize the event was generated by our own bot. It treated it as a new user message and bounced it straight back to the chat channels! 

**Bug 2: ClickUp only receives text and no files for Slack attachments**
Slack attachments sent to ClickUp were failing to upload because the ClickUp attachment API requires a valid file extension to determine the file type. Slack's iOS and web interface often generate extensionless filenames (like `Image from iOS`). When our backend relayed these to ClickUp, ClickUp rejected the upload entirely, throwing an error and only leaving the text comment.

### Implementation Changes

1. **Fixed ClickUp Loop Bouncing**: 
   - Modified [src/platforms/clickup-api.js](file:///e:/TDC_App/TDGAMES_App/Sync_Slack_Discord_ClickUp_Drive/src/platforms/clickup-api.js) to prepend `[SYNC] ` to the filenames of attachments right before uploading them to ClickUp.
   - Updated the [src/webhooks/clickup.js](file:///e:/TDC_App/TDGAMES_App/Sync_Slack_Discord_ClickUp_Drive/src/webhooks/clickup.js) webhook handler to scan the attachments in webhook payloads. If all attachments begin with the `[SYNC] ` prefix, the entire webhook payload gets skipped, perfectly eliminating the duplication loop on Discord and Slack!

2. **Fixed Extensionless Slack Filenames**:
   - Modified the [downloadAttachments](file:///e:/TDC_App/TDGAMES_App/Sync_Slack_Discord_ClickUp_Drive/src/relay.js#182-218) function in [src/relay.js](file:///e:/TDC_App/TDGAMES_App/Sync_Slack_Discord_ClickUp_Drive/src/relay.js) to inject missing file extensions. It checks if the filename contains a `.`, and if not, it uses the extracted `contentType` (e.g. `image/png` -> `.png`, `image/jpeg` -> `.jpg`) from the downloaded Slack file header. This satisfies the ClickUp Attachment API requirements.

### Files Modified Summary
- [src/platforms/clickup-api.js](file:///e:/TDC_App/TDGAMES_App/Sync_Slack_Discord_ClickUp_Drive/src/platforms/clickup-api.js): Prepended `[SYNC]` to filename on upload.
- [src/webhooks/clickup.js](file:///e:/TDC_App/TDGAMES_App/Sync_Slack_Discord_ClickUp_Drive/src/webhooks/clickup.js): Extracted attachments array earlier and implemented logic to catch and skip `[SYNC]` bounced attachments.
- [src/relay.js](file:///e:/TDC_App/TDGAMES_App/Sync_Slack_Discord_ClickUp_Drive/src/relay.js): Enhanced [downloadAttachments](file:///e:/TDC_App/TDGAMES_App/Sync_Slack_Discord_ClickUp_Drive/src/relay.js#182-218) to use `contentType` to give extensionless files a proper format for ClickUp's parser.

